Package: fathom
Title: See What Is in a JSON Document Before You Parse It
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("psychometrician", email = "psychometrician@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: One verb that describes an unknown JSON document: whether it is
    sound, what shapes it holds, and what one row could be, with each candidate
    priced. Output is proportional to the structure rather than to the data, so
    a 912 MB file and a 12 KB file produce descriptions of similar size. This
    package is a thin wrapper around the 'fathom' command-line engine, which it
    invokes as a subprocess. The engine is compiled and bundled into the package
    at install time, so an installed copy is self-contained.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
URL: https://github.com/psychometrician/fathom,
    https://psychometrician.github.io/fathom-book/
BugReports: https://github.com/psychometrician/fathom/issues
